      "writtenOn": "2021-10-12T16:34:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With how I had defined kDeviceSpaceShape, it was needed because the Shape passed into drawShape() is defined in device space, but you\u0027re right that if the paint doesn\u0027t have local coords then there\u0027d be no need to map with the inverse matrix to get those local coords (which I was planning to handle further down the stack).\n\nI have since moved back to older version of drawPaint that computes a covering rect in local space, which gives us the local coords and keeps all the draws in the same coord space.",
      "parentUuid": "d7c8da28_17110c05",
      "range": {
