      "writtenOn": "2021-10-08T22:14:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I dislike SkStrokeRec.\n\nI wonder if we can reconsider making our own StrokeRec.\n\n- fResScale is hacky, takes up space, and as you said, we should use the matrix cache instead. Tessellation doesn\u0027t use fResScale anyway.\n- The packed values aren\u0027t performant.\n- We can save space by representing join and miter limit in a single float.\n\nCould we instead put kStroke and kFill on the DrawFlags? Then our new SkStrokeRec would really just be the actual stroke params.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 140,
        "startChar": 42,
        "endLine": 140,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "67fdd00b3567086f0aef5f7114ccb6cba861e05e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
