    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "79b752b9_368a1cfe",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/Device.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 135,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-12T16:34:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah the Device will either hold the clip state or encapsulate it in some ClipStack class that I need to bring over still.\n\nFor now I want to hold off on doing any shape modification like this. I think it\u0027s most beneficial if it means that any analytic clip element doesn\u0027t need to apply at all, but if we have that super restricted (for now just a scissor) it\u0027s probably not worth it.\n\nI could see the CPU overhead of computing the intersection shapes taking up more time over N draws than the cost of drawing the clip once. If we get to doing 1 analytic rect, or 1 analytic rrect + clipping planes for a quality or non-dmsaa triggering POV, then the equation might change. I don\u0027t think it would be hard to adjust this function to modify the shape though.",
      "parentUuid": "b4a1d30f_090e0eb6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 135,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 135,
        "endChar": 19
